'' -Wl, as fbc has it: the value is split at commas, each piece reaches the linker as one
'' argument (here through clang's -Xlinker), after the runtime and the system libraries,
'' and repeated -Wl options accumulate -- measured on fbc-modern 2026-10-13 with -v. The
'' first piece is real: lld-link's /STACK, read back below as the program runs. On Linux
'' the same option carries '-rpath,$ORIGIN' (book work item T99).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -v -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/link-wl.bas -o tests/driver/linkwl.exe -Wl /STACK:8388608,/NXCOMPAT -Wl /DYNAMICBASE
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: -Xlinker /INCLUDE:tkort_msvc_init_ -Xlinker "/STACK:8388608" -Xlinker "/NXCOMPAT" -Xlinker "/DYNAMICBASE"
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/linkwl.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/linkwl.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: linked
